{"content":"q28.\n\n**Background workers actually started by the server** (in `server/server.go`, `startBackgroundRunners`, called from `Server.Start` at `server/server.go:129`):\n\n- **s3presign runner** (`server/runner/s3presign.Runner`, `server/runner/s3presign/runner.go`) — started at `server/server.go:162-169`. Trigger: runs once immediately (`RunOnce` at server.go:163), then a `time.NewTicker(runnerInterval)` with `runnerInterval = 12 * time.Hour` (`server/runner/s3presign/runner.go:27,30`) drives repeated `RunOnce`/`CheckAndPresign` calls inside `Run(ctx)` until its context is canceled on shutdown.\n\nThat's the only runner wired into `startBackgroundRunners` — no other goroutine loop is started from `server.NewServer`/`Server.Start`/`cmd/memos/main.go` (the other `go func()` sites are just the HTTP `Serve` call at server.go:124 and the shutdown-signal listener in `cmd/memos/main.go:99`).\n\n**Unused scheduling infrastructure:**\n- `server/runner/memopayload.Runner` (`server/runner/memopayload/runner.go`) — has its own `RunOnce` batch-rebuild logic, but `memopayload.NewRunner`/`Runner.RunOnce` is never called anywhere in the codebase (confirmed via reference search — the only production use of the `memopayload` package is the plain function `memopayload.RebuildMemoPayload`, called synchronously and per-request from `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:108,447`, not through the `Runner`/scheduling path). So this runner is defined but never started as a background job.\n- `internal/scheduler` package (`internal/scheduler/scheduler.go`, `job.go`, `parser.go`, etc.) — a full cron-style job scheduler (\"GitHub Actions-inspired cron job scheduler\", `internal/scheduler/doc.go:1`) with `scheduler.New()`, `Register`, cron-expression parsing, middleware, timezone support. It is exercised only by its own test files (`example_test.go`, `integration_test.go`) — `scheduler.New` has zero non-test call sites in the repo. The server does not use this package at all; the only actual scheduling mechanism in production is the plain `time.NewTicker` inside the s3presign runner.","iteration":11,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
